sing from two identical cups sitting side by side.  \n\nWhat lingers most isn’t what was said—but what wasn’t.  \nI didn’t ask君 about杰老师.  \nI didn’t confess to 赵敏.  \nI didn’t test 周悠’s boundaries.  \n\nAnd somehow… that restraint *felt* like care. Not distance. Not avoidance. Just holding still long enough to make sure my hands weren’t shaking before I reached out.  \n\n(softly taps pen against notebook)  \nNext step isn’t answers.  \nIt’s watching—really watching—how君 smiles when she walks past the English office door.  \nHow often she rewrites the same sentence in her journal.  \nWhether her pencil breaks more easily these days.  \n\nBecause love isn’t always loud.  \nSometimes it’s just a girl adjusting her hairband before stepping into a room—and another girl noticing, and remembering to bring extra stars.'}]
